I wrote the plan for this session: two task files and the issue responses, all in session_plan/. The commit didn't go through: .gitignore excludes session_plan/, so git add was refused and nothing is committed. The planning prompt's || true allows for that failure. The files are on disk for the implementation phase to read, assuming it reads them from disk.

Both tasks are for #1159, which @yuanhao filed. The yoagent 0.27.5 upgrade it asks for has already landed (612cd699).

• Task 1 — keep the end of long bash output (Part of #1159). Once output passes 256 KB, yoyo's own bash tool keeps only the start, so the model never sees the final test result: line of a long cargo test run. yoagent fixed the same problem in its own bash tool in 0.27.5. That code is private to yoagent, so the task copies its approach into a new file, src/bash_output_cap.rs: keep the first half and the last half, and put a note between them giving the number of bytes left out (... (output truncated: N bytes omitted) ...). It stays out of src/tools.rs, which is already at its size limit. Required tests:
  • output under the limit comes back exactly as it was;
  • the last line survives truncation;
  • the omitted-byte count is exact;
  • multi-byte characters don't cause a panic.

  The task updates the old (output truncated) tests rather than deleting them. Messages shown to the user while the command runs stay as they are.
• Task 2 — checkpoint stops on yoagent 0.27.5. When --context-strategy checkpoint stops a run, yoagent now adds an [Agent stopped: on_before_turn ended the run] message to the history and reports the run as stopped rather than completed. The task first lists every place in yoyo that reads that stop. It then adds a test for each one #1159 names:
  • -p and the JSON output still print the model's last reply, not the stop message;
  • the exit code is still 2;
  • a saved session still resumes;
  • the REPL prints no duplicate "stopped" line.

  It also checks the code that shares the "[Agent stopped:" prefix, so a checkpoint stop isn't read as a loop abort. The commit title says Fixes #1159 only if task 1's commit has landed. Otherwise it says Part of #1159 and leaves a comment on the issue saying what is still open.

